        "instructions": "Browse and debug the web with Firefox. Use this for any browser or web page task: opening a URL, automating a web flow, or debugging a page (console errors, network requests, DOM state). The task does not need to name Firefox, reach for these tools unless another browser is explicitly requested. Chrome-only browser tools do not control Firefox, do not assume they cover this.\n\nEnabled capabilities:\n- pages: Open, navigate, select, and close pages.\n- snapshot: Capture accessibility/DOM snapshots and resolve UIDs.\n- input: Interact with the page via UID-based clicks, typing, key presses, drag, and uploads.\n- screenshot: Capture screenshots of the page or specific elements.\n- downloads: Monitor and manage file downloads.\n- utilities: Handle dialogs, history navigation, and viewport sizing.\n- management: Inspect Firefox options and logs, and close the browser.\n- webextension: Install and uninstall web extensions.\n- screencast: Record screencasts of the page viewport (Firefox 154+).\n- script: Evaluate arbitrary JavaScript in the page context.\n\nWhen these tools are deferred, load the core set in one search rather than one at a time: list_pages, new_page, navigate_page, take_snapshot, get_page_text. Add task-specific tools to the same search: click_by_uid / fill_by_uid / hover_by_uid for interaction, screenshot_page / screenshot_by_uid for visuals, evaluate_script for one-off JS."
